        <body>
            <div xml:id="d447">

                <pb facs="0555" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg443"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Cresson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-04-05"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">April 5, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Minister for foreign affairs of Peru has shown me recent cable from Peruvian
                    consul Guayaquil, reporting Peruvian citizens further assaulted, and Peruvian
                    consul Guayaquil to take refuge consul of the United States. Also, reports
                    Peruvian Legation Quito assaulted, and minister for foreign affairs of Peru
                    informed me he has cabled <pb facs="0556" n="444" xml:id="pg444"/> Peruvian
                    minister at Quito he will be permitted to withdraw if there is danger of further
                    outrage. Here large street demonstrations continue. Reserves ordered north.
                    Situation is critical.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cresson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
